<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13284" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Derbē</span></b> , es, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δέρβη</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a fortified city of Lycaonia, residence of
				Cicero's friend, the tyrant Antipater; a place of refuge for
				Christians under persecution</i>, now Divlé, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act.
				14, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">16, 1</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Der-bes</span></b> ,
			ētis, or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Derbētes</span></b> , ae, m.,
				<i>an inhabitant of Derbe</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				13, 73, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Derbēus</span></b> ,
				ēi, m. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δερβαῖος</span>), of Derbe, Gaius, <i><span class="en">Vulg. Act.
				20, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
